    quiz: [
      { text: 'A client assumes Georgia is visa-free for Indian passport holders, like Mauritius. What is the accurate correction?', options: ['Correct, it is fully visa-free', 'Incorrect — an e-visa is required, though it is a straightforward online process with typical processing of a few business days', 'Incorrect — no visa option exists for Indian citizens at all', 'A visa is only required for stays over 90 days'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client worried about safety asks about Georgia\'s proximity to Russia and disputed border regions. What is the accurate, balanced guidance?', options: ['Georgia should be avoided entirely due to constant border conflict', 'The standard tourist circuit (Tbilisi, Kazbegi, Kakheti, Batumi) is geographically distant from the disputed Abkhazia/South Ossetia regions and unaffected, though checking current advisories close to departure is good practice', 'There are no border disputes affecting Georgia at all', 'Only Batumi is affected by border tensions'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A wine-interested client who has already toured France and Italy asks what makes Kakheti distinct. What is the strongest lesson-based answer?', options: ['Kakheti wine is identical to French wine in method and history', 'Georgia is widely considered the birthplace of winemaking with an 8,000-year continuous tradition using the distinctive qvevri clay-vessel method — a genuinely older, different story than Western European wine regions', 'Kakheti has no distinct winemaking tradition', 'Wine tasting is not available in Georgia'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client wants to drive themselves from Tbilisi to Kazbegi to see Mount Kazbek. What should you flag about this route?', options: ['The route is a flat, straight highway with no concerns', 'The Georgian Military Highway is scenic but winding through mountain terrain, which should be flagged for clients prone to motion sickness', 'This route does not exist and Kazbegi is unreachable by road', 'The drive takes over 15 hours each way'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client asks about direct flights from India to Tbilisi. What is the accurate guidance?', options: ['Extensive direct flights are available from all major Indian cities', 'Direct flights are limited and largely seasonal; most itineraries connect via Gulf hubs or Istanbul, adding a layover that should be stated explicitly in the quote', 'No flights of any kind connect India and Georgia', 'Only cargo flights operate on this route'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client wants a genuine adventure/ski add-on beyond the standard sightseeing circuit. What should you recommend?', options: ['Georgia has no ski or adventure infrastructure', 'Gudauri, which becomes a ski destination Dec–Mar, offering a genuine dual-season selling point most clients don\'t expect from this destination', 'Batumi, for its ski slopes', 'Kakheti, which is exclusively a winter sports destination'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'What should a client expect regarding accommodation quality in Kazbegi/Stepantsminda compared to Tbilisi?', options: ['Identical luxury-tier hotels in both locations', 'Simpler, more guesthouse-style accommodation given the small mountain-town setting — a genuine mountain-village experience, not a luxury base, and should be set as a clear expectation', 'Kazbegi has no accommodation options at all', 'Kazbegi accommodation is more luxurious than Tbilisi'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client asks what currency to use in Georgia. What is the accurate guidance?', options: ['Only US Dollars are accepted', 'The Georgian Lari (GEL); cards are widely accepted in Tbilisi and Batumi, while cash is more useful in smaller Kazbegi-area guesthouses and local markets', 'Euros are the official currency of Georgia', 'Indian Rupees are accepted directly throughout the country'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'What is the core value pitch that distinguishes Georgia from a full Western European itinerary?', options: ['Georgia offers no meaningful sightseeing compared to Europe', 'A "feels like Europe" experience — mountains, wine country, historic city culture — without Europe\'s visa complexity or price tag, given the low-friction e-visa and genuinely low cost of living', 'Georgia is more expensive than Western Europe', 'There is no meaningful difference between Georgia and Western Europe'], correctIndex: 1 },
      { text: 'A client wants to experience genuine local hospitality culture in Georgia. What should you mention?', options: ['Georgia has no distinctive hospitality traditions', 'The Georgian supra (feast) with its ritual toasting culture led by a tamada (toastmaster) is a genuine cultural institution worth mentioning, even if not required on a standard itinerary', 'Hospitality customs in Georgia are identical to those in Japan', 'Visitors are generally unwelcome in Georgian homes and gatherings'], correctIndex: 1 },
    ],
